The '''Tarsunt''' were a [[species]] of [[Hair|furry]] [[Sentience|sentients]] from the [[Tarsunt (planet)|planet of the same name]]. They were represented by [[Senator]] [[Colandrus]] in the [[Galactic Republic]], and by [[Lanever Villecham]] in the [[New Republic]]; the latter went on to serve as [[Chancellor (New Republic)|chancellor]] in the [[New Republic Senate]] until his [[death]] in the [[Hosnian Cataclysm]].

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|Times like this, it's good to have fur. Don't know how you humans do it.|Brill, to [[Thane Kyrell]]|<ref name="Lost Stars" />}}
[[File:VoberDand-CGSWG.png|thumb|250px|left|Vober Dand served the Resistance on D'Qar and later during their escape.]]
Tarsunts had long pelts of fur sprouting around their heads, some with brown coloration and elder members of the species exhibiting wispy white hair hanging long from the chin and jowls like a beard. They had large faces with broad brows, widely-spaced black eyes, a pair of large, flared nostrils, and hanging jowls over the mouth and chin, all framed by fur. Skin colors ranged from gray-blues to yellows<ref name="TFA VD" /> and purples.<ref name="Swoop Racers" /> Tarsunt [[Vober Dand]] stood at 1.73 [[meter]]s, and wore five-fingered [[glove]]s<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> over his paws.<ref name="Lost Stars" />

==Society and culture==
Signs of age were respected in Tarsunt culture.<ref name="TFA VD" /> Members of the species could speak [[Galactic Basic Standard]].<ref name="Lost Stars" />

==History==
Tarsunts were native to the planet Tarsunt,<ref name="Geektionary" /> of the [[Tarsunt system]] in the [[Mid Rim Territories]].<ref name="TFA VD" /> Some members of the species, such as Vober Dand, hailed from [[Suntilla]],<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> and the [[Suntilla system]] was represented by [[Senator]] [[Colandrus]] in the [[Galactic Senate]].<ref name="Obi-Wan & Anakin 3" />

==Tarsunts in the galaxy==
[[Veeth Drellik]]<ref name="AcolyteVG">''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> served as the [[Supreme Chancellor]] of the Galactic Republic in [[132 BBY]].<ref name="TA (episode)">''{{Acolyte|The Acolyte (episode)}}''</ref>

[[Blik (Tarsunt)|Blik]] ran a [[Unidentified gladiatorial arena|gladiatorial arena]] where [[droid]]s fought each other.<ref name="Always Bet on Chop">{{RebelsMagCite|23|Always Bet on Chop}}</ref>

[[Brill]] was a Tarsunt who served in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] as an [[engineer]], and participated in the [[Battle of Endor]]. She [[Hair dye|dyed]] her long pelt a shocking pink color.<ref name="Lost Stars" />

[[Lanever Villecham]] represented his [[homeworld]] of Tarsunt in the [[New Republic Senate]],<ref name="Geektionary" /> and was elected as [[Chancellor (New Republic)|chancellor]] of the [[New Republic]] in [[33 ABY]].<ref name="TFA VD" />

[[Vober Dand]], a brown-pelted Tarsunt from Suntilla, held the rank of chief of the [[Resistance]]'s [[Ground Logistics Division]] on [[D'Qar]], and used his mathematical mind to calculate flight schedules, maintenance requirements, and [[hangar]] operations.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> Although Vober's father, [[Ibdun Dand]], initially forbade him from joining the Resistance, the elder Tarsunt later joined his son in the [[Resistance ground crew]], and they served together on [[Ajan Kloss]] around the time of the [[Battle of Exegol]].<ref name="TROS VD" />

